# Architecture — {{project.name}}

> Kiro steering: architecture rules and patterns.

## Pattern: Onion Architecture

```
Presentation → Application + Infrastructure (DI only)
Infrastructure → Application + Domain + Common
Application → Domain + Common
Domain → Common
Common → nothing
```

## Pattern: CQRS via MediatR

```csharp
// ViewModel dispatches
await _mediator.Send(new CreateOrderCommand(name));
var orders = await _mediator.Send(new GetOrdersQuery());

// Handler implements
public sealed class CreateOrderCommandHandler : IRequestHandler<CreateOrderCommand, Guid>
{
    public async Task<Guid> Handle(CreateOrderCommand request, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        var order = Order.Place(request.CustomerId, request.Lines);  // domain
        await _repository.AddAsync(order, ct);                        // infrastructure
        return order.Id;
    }
}
```

## Pattern: MVVM

```csharp
public partial class OrdersViewModel : ViewModelBase
{
    [ObservableProperty] private IReadOnlyList<OrderDto> _orders = [];

    [RelayCommand(CanExecute = nameof(IsNotBusy))]
    private async Task LoadOrdersAsync()
    {
        IsBusy = true;
        Orders = await _mediator.Send(new GetOrdersQuery());
        IsBusy = false;
    }
    private bool IsNotBusy => !IsBusy;
}
```

## Never Do

- Domain referencing Application, Infrastructure, or Presentation
- ViewModel calling a repository directly
- Business logic in XAML code-behind
- Public setters on domain entities
